        "note": "How far you must go down from a peak before you can climb to a higher one."
      },
      {
        "id": "the-ripple",
        "label": "A ripple on a flank",
        "focus": [
          "ripple",
          "alone"
        ],
        "note": "A ripple high on a large peak has almost no prominence. A small peak alone in a valley has a great deal."
      },
      {
        "id": "drift",
        "label": "Why a drifting level is safe",
        "focus": [
          "drift"
        ],
        "note": "Prominence does not care where the signal sits, thus a threshold in prominence holds over a whole recording."
      }
    ]
